      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In rats maintained for 50 days on a low-sodium diet and with a compensatory hyperactivity of the renin-angiotensin system, the antinociceptive activity of morphine was significantly longer-lasting than in controls. It is suggested that the renin-angiotensin system modulates opioid system responsivity."},
